{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "32463328",
      "title": "Building a First Standalone Component",
      "lectureOrder": 665,
      "videoOrder": 612,
      "sourceHash": "213c2f65a9345cd8d4348a87f039f8cc26ae6c93c1b0180ee04dc12ac6fc1d41",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "Instructor: So how are standalone components built?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 7.05,
          "en": "Well, it turns out that you just build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.05,
          "end": 10.11,
          "en": "a regular component as you already know it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.11,
          "end": 13.98,
          "en": "and then you add a special property, a special flag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.98,
          "end": 18,
          "en": "to the object that is passed to the @Component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18,
          "end": 19.8,
          "en": "And that's the standalone flag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.8,
          "end": 22.833,
          "en": "which is a Boolean, which should be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 26.79,
          "en": "False is the default and does not have to be added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.79,
          "end": 30.06,
          "en": "True sets this to be a standalone component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 34.23,
          "en": "And internally, this will change many things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.23,
          "end": 36.75,
          "en": "because now this component can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "in other components without declaring it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 44.49,
          "en": "though you still need to make Angular aware of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.49,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "If you change this to true, and you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 50.37,
          "en": "you will note that now the app fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "It fails because this is now a standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 56.94,
          "en": "but it is still declared an NgModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.94,
          "end": 58.293,
          "en": "and that is wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.25,
          "end": 61.65,
          "en": "because now when you switch this to standalone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.65,
          "end": 65.16,
          "en": "you should no longer declare such a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.16,
          "end": 69.513,
          "en": "in this case the details component, in any NgModules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.44,
          "end": 72.57,
          "en": "So therefore here we should get rid of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.57,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "remove it from the declarations array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "and remove the import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "With that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "it kind of works, but it's actually gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "We no longer see the details part down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 87.72,
          "en": "Now we also don't see an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.72,
          "end": 90.33,
          "en": "in the console, but it's gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.33,
          "end": 91.5,
          "en": "The reason for that is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.5,
          "end": 94.68,
          "en": "it's actually not yet known by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.68,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "Now, all Angular sees is that in the welcome component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 101.07,
          "en": "there is an unknown HTML element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.07,
          "end": 104.00999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore it does not output anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.00999999999999,
          "end": 108.03,
          "en": "Because, yes, we as a developer know that DetailsComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 111.39,
          "en": "is the element or the component with that selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.39,
          "end": 113.49000000000001,
          "en": "but Angular doesn't know that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.49000000000001,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "Because even if you switch to standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 120.39,
          "en": "you still must make Angular aware of those components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.39,
          "end": 123.27,
          "en": "but you don't have to do it in a module anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.27,
          "end": 125.31,
          "en": "at least not necessarily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "Instead, what you have to do is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 129.78,
          "en": "you have to go to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.78,
          "end": 132.99,
          "en": "that should use this standalone component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.99,
          "end": 135.78,
          "en": "And of course, one standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 138.393,
          "en": "could be used in multiple components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.23,
          "end": 142.74,
          "en": "but here we only have one component that's using app-details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.74,
          "end": 144.42000000000002,
          "en": "and that's the welcome component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.42000000000002,
          "end": 146.49,
          "en": "So we have to go to that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.49,
          "end": 151.49,
          "en": "And there, we have to add an imports property to this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.52,
          "end": 155.043,
          "en": "that's passed to the component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.15,
          "end": 160.92000000000002,
          "en": "And here, we have to point at the standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.92000000000002,
          "end": 163.47,
          "en": "we want to use in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.47,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "So in this case, I want to use the details component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 169.77,
          "en": "hence I point at it by importing DetailsComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.77,
          "end": 170.94299999999998,
          "en": "and adding it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.07999999999998,
          "end": 174.75,
          "en": "However, you'll note that if I now save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.75,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "it indeed fails because this imports property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 181.26,
          "en": "can only be set if the welcome component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.26,
          "end": 184.443,
          "en": "is also a standalone component, which it is not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.43,
          "end": 188.79,
          "en": "Now we'll switch it to a standalone component in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.79,
          "end": 191.25,
          "en": "For the moment, let's instead get rid of that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.25,
          "end": 192.63,
          "en": "by commenting it out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.63,
          "end": 194.64,
          "en": "and let's find a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.64,
          "end": 196.2,
          "en": "Because I did mention before that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.2,
          "end": 199.17000000000002,
          "en": "one good thing about standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.17000000000002,
          "end": 202.41,
          "en": "is that you can combine them with NgModules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.41,
          "end": 206.01,
          "en": "so that you can migrate to standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.01,
          "end": 207.45,
          "en": "in a smooth way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.45,
          "end": 210,
          "en": "You don't have to rewrite your entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210,
          "end": 211.71,
          "en": "Instead, you can start switching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.71,
          "end": 214.59,
          "en": "individual components to standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.59,
          "end": 217.05,
          "en": "and still use them in your other components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.05,
          "end": 219.003,
          "en": "that are part of NgModules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.17000000000002,
          "end": 222.87,
          "en": "If you want to use a standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.87,
          "end": 226.07999999999998,
          "en": "in the various components that make up a module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.07999999999998,
          "end": 229.44,
          "en": "all you have to do is go to that module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.44,
          "end": 231.57,
          "en": "in this case, the app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 234.81,
          "en": "and now instead of adding the standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.81,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "here to declarations, you add it to imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 241.56,
          "en": "In the past, you typically added other modules here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.56,
          "end": 245.04,
          "en": "Now, with the introduction of these standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.04,
          "end": 246.9,
          "en": "directives, and pipes feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.9,
          "end": 250.95,
          "en": "you add all your standalone components, directives or pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.95,
          "end": 254.34,
          "en": "that should be usable by the other components of this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.34,
          "end": 256.86,
          "en": "here to this imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.86,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "So in this case, DetailsComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 262.2,
          "en": "which now also must be imported here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 262.2,
          "end": 265.383,
          "en": "It's imported and then added to imports here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.61,
          "end": 268.59,
          "en": "With that, everything compiles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 268.59,
          "end": 271.23,
          "en": "and we see our standalone component again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 272.88,
          "en": "And if I open the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 272.88,
          "end": 275.58,
          "en": "you see that clicks are also still registered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 275.58,
          "end": 279.69,
          "en": "and all of that works except for the custom directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 279.69,
          "end": 283.83,
          "en": "That does not work; the highlighting is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 283.83,
          "end": 287.37,
          "en": "Now, we'll fix this in a second, but before we fix it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.37,
          "end": 289.74,
          "en": "let me come back to this app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 289.74,
          "end": 292.53,
          "en": "What's the idea of standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 292.53,
          "end": 294.72,
          "en": "if we still have to add them here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 294.72,
          "end": 296.64,
          "en": "I mean, the only thing that changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 296.64,
          "end": 299.25,
          "en": "is that we now add them in a different place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 299.25,
          "end": 300.84,
          "en": "here in the app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 300.84,
          "end": 303.6,
          "en": "and we now actually have more code to write,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 303.6,
          "end": 306.6,
          "en": "because we did have to add this standalone flag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 306.6,
          "end": 308.28,
          "en": "to the details component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 308.28,
          "end": 309.99,
          "en": "Well, this is only the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 309.99,
          "end": 312.27,
          "en": "because this standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 312.27,
          "end": 314.52,
          "en": "only gets used in one other component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 314.52,
          "end": 316.92,
          "en": "which is part of an NgModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 316.92,
          "end": 320.13,
          "en": "So we're in the middle of a migration process here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 320.13,
          "end": 324.27,
          "en": "It will be less code if you only have standalone components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 324.27,
          "end": 326.64,
          "en": "or if you have a standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 326.64,
          "end": 330.18,
          "en": "that's used in a bunch of other standalone components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 330.18,
          "end": 332.73,
          "en": "Here we have the worst of both worlds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 332.73,
          "end": 335.4,
          "en": "so we didn't actually gain anything yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 335.4,
          "end": 338.34000000000003,
          "en": "but we'll get there over the next minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 338.34000000000003,
          "end": 341.73,
          "en": "This is, however, how we can add such a standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.73,
          "end": 344.31,
          "en": "and therefore in the essence, all you have to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 344.31,
          "end": 348.54,
          "en": "is set this flag and then add it to imports:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 348.54,
          "end": 352.984,
          "en": "here in an NgModule, or if WelcomeComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 352.984,
          "end": 355.29,
          "en": "would be a standalone component itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 355.29,
          "end": 358.05,
          "en": "here, with help of imports, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 358.05,
          "end": 360.003,
          "en": "But that is something I'll get back to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 361.14,
          "end": 363.39,
          "en": "Before we get back to this, let's make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 363.39,
          "end": 366.063,
          "en": "that our custom directive is working again though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 366.93,
          "end": 369.72,
          "en": "Our custom directive is not working anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 369.72,
          "end": 372.33,
          "en": "because while I do still use it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 372.33,
          "end": 376.08,
          "en": "in the template of my details component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 376.08,
          "end": 379.02,
          "en": "this component is a standalone component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 379.02,
          "end": 383.07,
          "en": "and therefore decoupled from an NgModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 383.07,
          "end": 385.86,
          "en": "Yes, it still has to be imported there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 385.86,
          "end": 388.35,
          "en": "but it's not aware of any other things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 388.35,
          "end": 391.89,
          "en": "that might be made available by that module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 391.89,
          "end": 393.96,
